translated_text:
BY THE GRACE OF GOD ALMIGHTY

REGENT OF KONAWE KEPULAUAN,
a. that every citizen has the right to be free from torture or treatment that degrades human dignity and has the right to obtain a sense of security and freedom from all forms of violence;
b. that protection of women and children victims of violence is one aspect of the duties and responsibilities of the regional government as mandated by law in providing protection and services to the community;
c. that the Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 1 of 2010 concerning Minimum Service Standards in the Field of Integrated Services for women and children victims of violence, it is necessary to regulate the handling of women and children victims of violence in the region;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letters a, b, and c above, it is deemed necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence;

Bearing in mind: 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 4 of 1979 concerning Children (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1979 Number 32, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3243);
3. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3835);
4. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235., as has been amended several times most recently by Law Number 17 of 2016 concerning the Stipulation of Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 1 of 2016 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 99, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5882);
5. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
6. Law Number 11 of 2009 concerning Social Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2009 Number 12, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6967);
7. Law Number 13 of 2013 concerning the Establishment of Konawe Kepulauan Regency in Southeast Sulawesi Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2013 Number 84, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5415);

8. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 5587), as has been amended several times by Law Number 11 of 2021 Concerning Job Creation (State Gazette of 2020 Number 245 Supplement to the State Gazette Number 6573);
9. Government Regulation Number 44 of 2017 concerning the Implementation of Child Care (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2017 Number 220, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6132);

With Mutual Approval

